From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
Subject: [PATCH] SPARC64: list the whole virtual address space in
 /virtual-memory available

Since 6e3d3fd ("libopenbios: limit upper virtual memory range to
ofmem_arch_get_virt_top()") the "available" property of /virtual-memory
ends at 0xff000000. Claims above that address are not shown in it, and
64-bit Solaris maps its kernel heap there: Solaris 10 (1/13) claims about
180 pages at 0x30000000000 and up through the boot program before the
kernel takes over the firmware's translations.

Solaris sizes the pool of "nucleus" hme blocks that it takes those
translations over into from the holes between the entries of that list
(size_virtalloc() in startup_modules()). The heap pages were not holes in
the list, the pool was too small, and Solaris 10 stopped with

  panic - kernel: no nucleus hblk8 to allocate

with 256 MB to 2 GB of RAM.

List the whole 64-bit space like OBP does instead, and claim the two
ranges that are never available: the firmware's own range from
OFMEM_VIRT_TOP to 4 GB, and the UltraSPARC I/II VA hole from
0x0000080000000000 to 0xfffff80000000000. OBP leaves the hole out of the
list too, and Solaris subtracts it when it finds it there. Claims with an
alignment still search below OFMEM_VIRT_TOP only.

6e3d3fd limited the list because Solaris 9 stopped with "VAC too big!"
with the whole space in it. That panic comes later in Solaris's startup
than the one the limit leads to (BOP_ALLOC failed in startup_memlist()),
and its cause is the CPU node's icache-size (fixed separately), not this
list: with this change and that fix Solaris 9 gets past both.

With this Solaris 10 1/13 boots from its DVD to the installer's language
prompt on a serial console.
---
 arch/sparc64/ofmem_sparc64.c         |  7 +++++++
 include/arch/sparc64/ofmem_sparc64.h |  4 ++++
 libopenbios/ofmem_common.c           | 11 ++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/sparc64/ofmem_sparc64.c b/arch/sparc64/ofmem_sparc64.c
index 88b73b6..5abc78b 100644
--- a/arch/sparc64/ofmem_sparc64.c
+++ b/arch/sparc64/ofmem_sparc64.c
@@ -353,6 +353,13 @@ void ofmem_init( void )
 	memset(&s_ofmem_data, 0, sizeof(s_ofmem_data));
 	s_ofmem_data.ofmem.ramsize = qemu_mem_size;
 
+	/* Keep the firmware's own range above OFMEM_VIRT_TOP and the
+	   UltraSPARC I/II VA hole out of the available list, as OBP does:
+	   the list covers the whole 64-bit space, and Solaris sizes its pool
+	   of nucleus hme blocks from the holes in it */
+	ofmem_claim_virt(OFMEM_VIRT_TOP, 0x100000000ULL - OFMEM_VIRT_TOP, 0);
+	ofmem_claim_virt(VA_HOLE_START, VA_HOLE_END - VA_HOLE_START, 0);
+
 	/* inherit translations set up by entry.S */
 	ofmem_walk_boot_map(remap_page_range);
 
diff --git a/include/arch/sparc64/ofmem_sparc64.h b/include/arch/sparc64/ofmem_sparc64.h
index 19f2747..4bdfc6a 100644
--- a/include/arch/sparc64/ofmem_sparc64.h
+++ b/include/arch/sparc64/ofmem_sparc64.h
@@ -18,6 +18,10 @@
 
 #define OFMEM_VIRT_TOP 0xff000000
 
+/* UltraSPARC I/II implement 44 virtual address bits: the hole between */
+#define VA_HOLE_START  0x0000080000000000ULL
+#define VA_HOLE_END    0xfffff80000000000ULL
+
 #define PAGE_SIZE_4M   (4 * 1024 * 1024)
 #define PAGE_SIZE_512K (512 * 1024)
 #define PAGE_SIZE_64K  (64 * 1024)
diff --git a/libopenbios/ofmem_common.c b/libopenbios/ofmem_common.c
index fc19d27..e86eefd 100644
--- a/libopenbios/ofmem_common.c
+++ b/libopenbios/ofmem_common.c
@@ -349,8 +349,17 @@ static void ofmem_update_translations( void )
 
 	ofmem_update_memory_available(s_phandle_memory, ofmem->phys_range, 
 			&phys_range_prop, &phys_range_prop_size, &phys_range_prop_used, get_ram_size() - 1);
-	ofmem_update_memory_available(s_phandle_mmu, ofmem->virt_range, 
+#ifdef CONFIG_SPARC64
+	/* The whole 64-bit address space, as OBP lists it: the firmware's own
+	   range and the VA hole are claimed in ofmem_init(), and claims above
+	   ofmem_arch_get_virt_top() (Solaris maps its 64-bit kernel heap there)
+	   must show up as holes in the list */
+	ofmem_update_memory_available(s_phandle_mmu, ofmem->virt_range,
+			&virt_range_prop, &virt_range_prop_size, &virt_range_prop_used, (ucell)-1);
+#else
+	ofmem_update_memory_available(s_phandle_mmu, ofmem->virt_range,
 			&virt_range_prop, &virt_range_prop_size, &virt_range_prop_used, ofmem_arch_get_virt_top() - 1);
+#endif
 	ofmem_update_mmu_translations();
 }
 
